      "id": 1,
      "text": "Mountain man Jim Bridger and Louis Vasquez established Fort Bridger in 1842 as a fur trading outpost on the Green River.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        4,
        7
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fort_Bridger"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "Fort Bridger became a vital resupply point for wagon trains traveling along the Oregon, California, and Mormon Trails.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        18
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fort_Bridger"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "During the 1860s, Fort Bridger served as a station for the Pony Express, the Overland Stage, and the transcontinental telegraph.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        17
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.nps.gov/mopi/planyourvisit/fort-bridger.htm"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "The United States Army established a military post at Fort Bridger in 1858 during the Utah War.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        19
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fort_Bridger"
    },
    {
